# Copy to .env.local and fill in from your Supabase project:
#   Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API
#
# .env.local is gitignored. This file is the only committed env file, and it
# MUST never contain real values.
#
# Both variables are PUBLIC by design: they are inlined into the browser bundle
# and are safe to expose. Access control is enforced by Postgres RLS, not by
# hiding these (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §1).
#
# There is deliberately NO service-role key here. RedyQuote uses none anywhere
# (docs/TECH-STACK.md §6) — every database access runs under a real user's
# session. If you ever find yourself adding one, update TECH-STACK.md first.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
